hadiths[31]{hadithnumber,text}:
"813","On the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with them, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went to bed, he would sleep on his right side, then he said: “O Allah, I surrender myself to You, turn my face to You, entrust my affairs to You, and turn my back to You, out of desire and fear for You. There is no refuge or place of safety from You except in You. I believe in Your Book which You have revealed, and in Your Prophet who “I was sent.” [Narrated by Al-Bukhari with this wording in the Book of Adab from his Sahih]"
"814","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) directed me thus: ""Whenever you go to bed, perform Wudu' as you do for Salat then (before sleeping) recite: 'O Allah! I have submitted myself to You, I have turned myself to You, committed my affairs to You and sought Your refuge for protection out of desire for You and fear of You (expecting Your reward and fearing Your punishment). There is no refuge and no place of safety from You but with You. I believe in the Book You have revealed and in the Prophet (ﷺ) You have sent.""' He also mentioned similar supplications, and in that narration, it is stated: ""Make these the last of what you say before sleeping."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"815","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Prophet (ﷺ) used to pray eleven rak’ahs at night, and when dawn came, he would pray two light rak’ahs, then lie on his right side until the muezzin came and called him to prayer [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"816","On the authority of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Prophet (ﷺ) went to bed at night, he would put his hand under his cheek, then say: “O Allah, in your name I die and live.” And when he woke up, he would say: “Praise be to Allah who brought us back to life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection” [Al-Bukhari]."
"817","My father said: I was lying down on my belly in the mosque when someone shook me with his foot and said, ""Lying down this way is disapproved by Allah."" I looked up and saw that it was Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). [Abu Dawud] ."
"818","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever sits in a seat in which Allah Almighty is not mentioned, there will be a deficiency from Allah Almighty, and whoever lies in a place in which Allah Almighty is not mentioned, there will be a liability from Allah” ([Abu Dawud]. The consequence."
"819","On the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, may Allah be pleased with him, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) lying in the mosque, placing one leg on top of the other. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"820","On the authority of Jabir bin Samra, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Prophet (ﷺ) prayed the dawn prayer, he would sit cross-legged in his seat until the beautiful sun rose. An authentic hadith, narrated by Abu Dawud and others with authentic chains of transmission."
"821","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the courtyard of the Kaaba, sitting in the squatting posture (qurfaṣ) with his hands placed like this. He explained that this posture with his hands is qurfaṣ (squatting with knees drawn up). [Al-Bukhari]."
"822","I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) seated with his arms enfolding his legs; and when I saw him in such a state of humble guise I trembled with fear due to the awe (he showed in that posture). [Abu Dawud and At-Tirmidhi] ."
"823","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by me when I was sitting with my left hand behind my back and leaning on my palm. On seeing me in this posture he said, ""Do you sit like those upon whom the Wrath of Allah has descended?"" [Abu Dawud] ."
"824","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “None of you should rise from his sitting place and then sit in it, but expand and make space.” And if Ibn Omar had a man rise up for him from his seat, he would not sit in it. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"825","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If one of you gets up from a meeting and then returns to it, he has more right to it.” [Muslim]."
"826","Whenever we came to the gathering of the Prophet, we would sit down at the end (of the assembly). [Abu Dawud and At-Tirmidhi] ."
"827","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""If a man takes a bath on Friday, purifies himself thoroughly, uses oil and perfume which is available in the house, sets forth for the mosque, does not (forcibly) sit between two persons, offers the prayer that is prescribed for him and listens to the Imam silently, his sins between this Friday and the previous Friday will be forgiven."" [Al- Bukhari] ."
"828","On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It is not permissible for a man to separate two men except with their permission.” It was narrated by Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi and he said, “A good hadith.” And in a narration by Abu Dawud: “He does not sit between two men except with their permission.”"
"829","The Messenger of Allah curses the one who sits in the middle of people's circle. [Abu Dawud] . A man sat in the middle of a circle so Hudhaifah (May Allah be pleased with him) said: Cursed is he who sits in the middle of the circle, on the tongue of Muhammad (ﷺ). [At-Tirmidhi] ."
"830","I heard Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying ""The best assemblies are those in which people make room for one another."" [Abu Dawud] ."
"831","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever sits in a gathering, and there is a lot of idle talk in it, and he says before he gets up from that sitting: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You, then he will be forgiven for whatever occurred in that sitting.” ([Al-Tirmidhi] A good and authentic hadith.)"
"832","On the authority of Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would say towards the end of his life when he wanted to get up from the assembly: “Glory be to Allah and with Your praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You.” Then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, are you saying something that you used to say in the past? He said: “That is atonement for what happened in the assembly.” [Abu Dawud].[Narrated by Al-Hakim Abu Ubaidullah in Al-Mustadrak from the narration of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, and he said: It is authentic with a chain of transmission]"
"833","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Rarely did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) rise from a gathering until he made these supplications: “O Allah, grant us from Your fear that which will come between us and your disobedience, and of your obedience that which will bring us to your paradise, and of certainty that which will make the calamities of this world easy for us. O Allah, grant us enjoyment with our hearing, sight, and strength as long as you give us life, and make it our heir. And make our vengeance against those who wronged us, and grant us victory over those who antagonized us, and do not make our calamity a part of our religion, and do not make this world our greatest concern, nor the extent of our knowledge, and do not make those who do not have mercy upon us dominate over us” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"834","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is no people who rises from a gathering and does not mention Allah Almighty in it except that they rise up from something like the carcass of a donkey, and they are saddened” [Abu Dawud]."
"835","And on the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “A people does not sit in a gathering in which they do not mention Allah Almighty, nor pray for their Prophet, except that they will have a blame (from Allah); if He wishes, He will punish them, and if He wishes, He will forgive them” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"836","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""If anyone sits in a gathering where he does not remember Allah, there will be upon him a blame from Allah, and he who lies down in a place where he does not remember Allah, will bring grief upon himself (on the Day of Resurrection)."" [Abu Dawud] ."
"837","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Nothing remains from the prophecy except the good tidings.” They said: What are the good tidings? He said: “The good vision” [Al-Bukhari]."
"838","On his authority, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “When the time approaches, the vision of the believer will hardly be false, and the vision of the believer is one of the forty-six parts of prophecy” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration: “The most truthful vision of you is the most truthful of speech.”"
"839","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever sees me in a dream will see me while awake - or as if he saw me while awake - Satan will not take my form” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"840","I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, ""When one of you sees a dream that he likes, then it is from Allah. He should praise Allah for it and relate it to (others)."" Another narration adds: Messenger of Allah(ﷺ) said, ""He should not report it except to those whom he loves. And if he sees one which he dislikes, then it is from the Satan. He should seek refuge in Allah against its evil and should not mention it to anyone. Then it will not harm him."" [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"841","On the authority of Abu Qatada, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “A good vision - and in one narration: a good vision - is from Allah, and a dream is from Satan, so whoever sees something that he hates, let him blow on his left hand three times, and seek refuge from Satan, for it will not harm him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. Blowing is gentle blowing without saliva"
"842","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “If one of you sees a vision that he hates, let him spit to his left three times, and let him seek refuge in Allah from Satan three times, and turn away from the side he was on” [Muslim]."
"843","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Of the worst lies are: to claim a false father, or to pretend to have seen what one has not seen (tell a false dream), or to attribute to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) what he has not said."" [Al-Bukhari] ."
